#Python ruleset

Use stable industry standards, but choose to allow modern updates if it helps the project be future facing.

## pep8
- adhere to pep8 as much as possible

## flake8
I have specified a [.flake8](mdc:.flake8) file with some helpful exceptions

## variables
- snake case for variables
- Camel case for Classes

## Type hints
- always use them

## Functions
- always type hint
- always docstring

# Object oriented vs procedural style
- I prefer a procedural style but want to leverage the power of classes and oop when it is appropriate. Minimize the inheritance hierarchy to keep things simple at first. 
- use pydantic to move data through the application where appropriate. When pydantic is used to model a data structure, update the [guidance.md](mdc:guidance.md) file.
- for data operations that occur in loops use object mapping, for one off data manipulations you can use SQL or Cypher or whatever the native query language is.

# Start explicit iterate to optimize
I'm not the brightest programmer, when initially developing code, prefer more explicit code solutions with inline comments to help me understand. Once the code is working, we can refactor for conciseness.



